<Concept title="Combat Combos" section="Mechanics">
  <p><em>Placeholder — not yet specified.</em></p>

  <h2>Scope</h2>
  <p>Will define normal and strong attack chains, the combo window timing (how long after a hit the next input chains), and how those windows vary per weapon type.</p>

  <h2>Implemented by</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>scripts/3d/player/player.gd</code> (Player) — <code>_start_attack</code> / <code>_start_strong_attack</code> begin or advance a combo (tracked by <code>combo_state</code>); <code>_handle_attack_state</code> opens the combo window at <code>COMBO_WINDOW_OPEN_PCT</code> of the swing and closes it after <code>COMBO_WINDOW_DURATION</code>; <code>_play_attack_animation</code> / <code>_play_and_track_attack</code> drive the per-step animation and SFX; <code>_activate_attack_hitbox</code> (melee) and <code>_fire_projectile</code> (ranged weapon types) apply the hit. Per-weapon <code>combo_steps</code> come from <code>CombatManager.get_weapon_type_config</code>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>These attacks are the ATTACKING state of the <a href="/states/player-state">Player State Machine</a>.</p>

  <p><a href="/mechanics">← Mechanics</a></p>
</Concept>
